the brutal attacks against ukrainian  citizens have horrified the world  the biden administration says it is  working with its allies to put russian  president vladimir putin on trial  ukraine has set up an online archive to  document the atrocities these are war  crimes these are shocking and brutal  acts that are completely unacceptable  and the united states will work with the  international community to make sure  there's accountability cell phones are  recording the brutality that has gone  beyond the usual boundaries of war  attacks on civilian targets allegations  of rape torture and extreme deprivation  all can constitute war crimes or crimes  against humanity captured russian  soldiers are reportedly saying they were  told to bomb civilian areas even handing  over maps we filed all the criminal  charges in the international court we  have the criminal cases opened in  ukraine more than 4 000 of individual  criminal cases already by the prosecutor  general we have 10 more countries that  open their own  individual criminal prosecutions and  we're providing all the evidence to them  along with putin ukraine officials are  vowing to prosecute soldiers and  military commanders both on the ground  and in russia international war crimes  investigators are in ukraine risking  their own lives to defend those whose  lives were savagely taken experts warn  evidence gathering is a slow task people  should be prepared for some time and the  complexity of the process that this is  not going to be immediate  and this is not going to be easy  no sitting head of state has ever been  tried for war crimes finding and  arresting a heavily protected vladimir  putin won't be easy but in-person  prosecution is required by international  law vladimir putin needs to be charged  and go to justice  or die with an indictment hanging over  his head  russia has repeatedly denied it has  committed any war crimes but the  evidence has been overwhelming and  broadcast all over the world  images that have haunted millions and  galvanized leaders from the u.s canada  and their allies to make putin pay  jennifer johnson global news washington
 

